      "10. Publish limitations beside every finding. For “How Do Clock Definitions Change Offshore Handoff Results?,” the protocol records the eligible population, source systems, timestamps, reviewer roles, first-pass classification, confidence, owner dependency, downstream consequence, and unavailable evidence. Stage 10 of cross-border-handoff-clock-semantics-study reports counts, denominators, exclusions, missingness, disagreement, correction, reversal, reopening, and unresolved status. Protected narratives remain in approved systems while analysis uses stable references and minimum-necessary fields. The method can characterize observed operating records; it cannot prove causation, legal compliance, universal provider quality, intent, or a promised business outcome. An accountable client owner decides whether the evidence supports a process change, and any remediation receives an owner, due date, implementation event, verification test, and residual limitation.",
      "Decision-use audit. For “How Do Clock Definitions Change Offshore Handoff Results?,” reviewers must show how a sensitivity study compares created, received, evidence-ready, accepted, acted, and destination-confirmed timestamps across time zones. The report ties each operational conclusion to a versioned source and declares which owner decision it can inform. It displays the eligible population, additions, transfers, withdrawals, unresolved items, and final population before presenting a rate. It also separates staff preparation time from owner waiting and system delay, because combining those intervals would direct remediation toward the wrong part of the offshore operating model.",
      "Adverse-case analysis. The cross-border-handoff-clock-semantics-study protocol includes an ordinary record, a missing source, a plausible conflict, a duplicate, an unavailable owner, a late correction, and an apparent success that fails destination verification. Reviewers preserve first-pass classifications and confidence before discussion. They explain whether disagreement concerns facts, population membership, consequence, authority, timing, or closure. A fresh case is used after any instruction changes so familiarity with one example cannot masquerade as a durable improvement in the control.",
      "Sensitivity plan. For “How Do Clock Definitions Change Offshore Handoff Results?,” analysts repeat the result under reasonable alternatives for time windows, pause rules, risk bands, exclusion criteria, unresolved cases, and missing evidence. Each alternative retains its numerator and denominator. When a conclusion reverses, the report identifies the responsible assumption and describes the result as sensitive instead of choosing the most reassuring specification. The protocol does not use one headline average to offset a rare unauthorized action involving identity, money, private data, privileged access, or an external customer commitment.",
      "Implementation and verification. Any recommendation from cross-border-handoff-clock-semantics-study becomes a bounded pilot with a named owner, eligible population, permission map, review date, rollback trigger, and destination-level success test. A revised checklist, meeting, training assignment, or favorable first example is not implementation evidence. The follow-up review samples fresh work, reports residual exceptions beside completed items, and confirms whether source quality, authority, timing, and downstream state improved. Client owners retain decisions about policy, access, disclosure, financial treatment, employment, contracts, and risk acceptance.",
      "Sources: https://www.nist.gov/cyberframework; https://www.nist.gov/privacy-framework; https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/53/r5/upd1/final; https://www.gao.gov/green-book; https://www.cisa.gov/cybersecurity-performance-goals; https://www.ftc.gov/business-guidance/resources/protecting-personal-information-guide-business; https://www.archives.gov/records-mgmt; https://www.census.gov/about/policies/quality/standards.html; https://www.bls.gov/opub/hom/; https://privacy.gov.ph/data-privacy-act/. Accessed 2026-10-13. These authoritative sources support governance, privacy, security, records, and statistical method; the declared protocol and client policy govern the specific study."
